# Copy to .env - which is gitignored - and fill in.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Both are read at runtime by server.mjs and served to the browser through
# /api/config, so a change here needs `docker compose up -d` and nothing more.
# No rebuild, and the same image works on any host.

# Google Drive backup. This is the *client ID*, not the client secret.
# It's public by design - it identifies the app, it doesn't authorise anything
# on its own, and it's visible in any browser's network tab. The browser sign-in
# flow is a public client and has no secret; if you were issued one, it isn't
# used here and shouldn't be stored anywhere.
#
# Setup: docs/google-drive-setup.md
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# Optional: Gemini text-to-speech. The browser voice is used without it.
#
# Unlike the client ID above, this one *is* a secret, and /api/config hands it
# to the browser - so anyone who can load the page can read it. Fine on a
# private network; think twice before exposing the app publicly with this set.
# Leaving it blank and letting people paste their own key under Settings avoids
# the problem entirely.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
